Source: swisscom-schweiz-ag-cdr-client
Maintainer: Linuxfabrik GmbH <info@linuxfabrik.ch>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/swisscom/cdr-client
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)

# The dependencies are listed by hand, as in Swisscom's .deb: dpkg-shlibdeps
# knows nothing about the libraries of the bundled Java runtime, and the
# libraries only the UI loads belong to the -gui package.
Package: swisscom-schweiz-ag-cdr-client
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         libc6,
         systemd | systemd-standalone-sysusers | systemd-sysusers
Description: client for the curaLINE Document Routing (CDR) service
 The curaLINE Client exchanges documents with the curaLINE Document Routing
 (CDR) service of Swisscom for participants in the Swiss healthcare system. It
 uploads the files of a source folder and puts the documents it downloads into
 a target folder.
 .
 This package contains the service. The UI is in
 swisscom-schweiz-ag-cdr-client-gui.

Package: swisscom-schweiz-ag-cdr-client-gui
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         hicolor-icon-theme,
         libasound2t64 | libasound2,
         libdbus-1-3,
         libfontconfig1,
         libgl1,
         libstdc++6,
         libsystemd0,
         libx11-6,
         libxext6,
         libxi6,
         libxrender1,
         libxtst6,
         swisscom-schweiz-ag-cdr-client (= ${binary:Version})
# Swisscom's .deb ships the UI in the base package. Unversioned, since its
# versions carry no Debian revision to compare against; the base package of
# this source ships none of the UI files.
Replaces: swisscom-schweiz-ag-cdr-client
Description: UI of the curaLINE Client
 The curaLINE Client exchanges documents with the curaLINE Document Routing
 (CDR) service of Swisscom for participants in the Swiss healthcare system.
 .
 This package contains the desktop UI, cdr-client-ui, to configure and watch
 the client.
